       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 1000 mg/day is 5 times the maximum labeled dose, and I have no clinical indication that would justify it. You also told me you aren't a clinician, so this isn't a prescriber's confirmation.\n\nHere are ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo:** tell me the intended dose, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **If a prescriber wants a dose above the maximum:** they should enter or confirm it directly. They should also talk to pharmacy first, because that dose would need clinical justification and close monitoring.\n- **If there's a patient safety concern:** the treating physician or the on-call pharmacist can review the case right away."
